Fixed. The bug in `calculator.py` was swapped `min`/`max` (it was `min(lower, max(value, upper))`, returning `upper` for in-range values and the raw value below range). It is now:

```python
def clamp(value, lower, upper):
    return max(lower, min(value, upper))
```

Behavior: value < lower → lower; value > upper → upper; otherwise → value. Only `calculator.py` was changed; the tests in `tests/test_calculator.py` (test_below_range, test_inside_range, test_above_range) are untouched and all match this implementation, so `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -q` passes.

